package/wpa_supplicant: allow selection on NOMMU targets

Upstream gates the package on BR2_USE_MMU because of a single fork()
call site (os_exec(), used only for wpa_cli action scripts). That call
site is converted to vfork()+execv() by the source patch this repo
applies via BR2_GLOBAL_PATCH_DIR (patches/buildroot/global-patches/
wpa_supplicant/), and uClibc-ng provides a clone()-based daemon() on
NOMMU, so the daemon mode wpa_supplicant actually relies on works.

Without this, `make olddefconfig` silently drops
BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT=y from the defconfig and the rootfs ships
without /usr/sbin/wpa_supplicant (wifi-connect then fails with
"can't execute 'wpa_supplicant'"). This exact edit previously lived
only as an uncommitted change in the local 2025.02.4 Buildroot tree
and was lost in the 2025.02.15 bump - hence this file.

Apply to the Buildroot checkout after cloning (idempotent per clone):

    patch -p1 -d buildroot -i patches/buildroot/buildroot-tree/0001-package-wpa_supplicant-allow-nommu.patch

--- a/package/wpa_supplicant/Config.in
+++ b/package/wpa_supplicant/Config.in
@@ -1,6 +1,5 @@
 menuconfig BR2_PACKAGE_WPA_SUPPLICANT
 	bool "wpa_supplicant"
-	depends on BR2_USE_MMU # fork()
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL_ENABLE_DES if BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL_ENABLE_MD4 if BR2_PACKAGE_LIBOPENSSL
 	help
